.Dd September 20, 2026
.Dt AMTR 1
.Os anthropometer 0.6.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm amtr
.Nd agentic debugger for Claude Code, Codex CLI and Gemini CLI sessions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo Fl -session Ar file | Ar id Oc
.Oo Fl -project Ar path Oc
.Oo Fl -budget Ar n Oc
.Oo Fl -theme Ar name Oc
.Oo Fl -engine Ar path Oc
.Oo Fl -python Ar path Oc
.Oo Fl -tour | Fl -no-tour Oc
.Oo Fl -engine-args Ar ARGS ... Oc
.Nm
.Fl -demo
.Sh DESCRIPTION
amtr attaches to a running or finished agent session and lets you debug it the way you would a process: the model's context window as a live memory map, what fills it and the actual text, a scrub back to any turn, the price of every call, each subagent's own window, and an autopsy of every compaction.
Pressing R compiles a ground-truth PDF report of the whole session.
.Pp
amtr is the terminal user interface; the numbers come from amtr_engine.py, a standard-library Python program that amtr spawns as a child.
The engine is found next to the binary, in ../lib/amtr, or through AMTR_ENGINE.
It can also be run on its own for a report on standard output (amtr_engine.py --report) or a headless session roster (--fleet).
.Pp
With no session given, amtr attaches to the newest session on the machine.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -session Ar file|id
Attach to a session: a Claude Code, Codex CLI or Gemini CLI transcript path, or its session id.
.It Fl -project Ar path
Attach to the newest session under this project path.
.It Fl -budget Ar n
Pin the context budget, in tokens; passed to the engine.
.It Fl -theme Ar name
Block theme.
The default is terminal.
One of terminal, ukiyo-e, bauhaus, mono.
.It Fl -engine Ar path
Path of amtr_engine.py.
The default is next to the binary, or $AMTR_ENGINE.
.It Fl -python Ar path
Python interpreter used to run the engine.
The default is python3.
.It Fl -engine-args Ar args ...
Everything after this flag goes to the engine's argv verbatim.
.It Fl -demo
Run a deterministic demo session with no engine: the reproducible scene source for visual and animation validation.
.It Fl -tour
Open the welcome tour at launch.
It opens by itself on the very first launch, and w reopens it any time.
.It Fl -no-tour
Never open the tour automatically.
.El
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 1-6
Switch tab.
.It f
Sessions list.
.It ?
Help.
.It w
Welcome tour.
.It Left, Right
Scrub through turns.
.It m
Map mode.
.It t
Cycle theme.
.It R
Compile the PDF report of the session.
.It q
Quit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev AMTR_ENGINE
Path of amtr_engine.py; the Homebrew wrapper sets it.
.It Ev AMTR_NO_TOUR
Set to 1 to suppress the welcome tour (scripted runs, recordings).
.It Ev AMTR_NO_FIT
Engine: disable the per-category chars-per-token fit and size every category with the single global constant.
.It Ev AMTR_SELF_SESSION
Engine: the session id to treat as amtr's own, so it is not listed as a target.
.It Ev AMTR_PROXY_BODIES
Engine, with --proxy: also record request bodies.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.claude/projects/*/*.jsonl
Claude Code transcripts, the primary input.
.It Pa ~/.codex/sessions/
Codex CLI transcripts.
.It Pa ~/.claude/amtr-reports/<name>-<id>/
Reports compiled with R.
.It Pa ~/.claude/amtr/welcomed
Marker that the first-launch tour has been shown.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Attach to the newest session on the machine:
.Dl $ amtr
.Pp
Attach to the newest session of one project:
.Dl $ amtr --project ~/Developer/whiskr
.Pp
Open a finished session by id, with the mono theme:
.Dl $ amtr --session 3f2c1a9e --theme mono
.Pp
A text report of a session, no interface:
.Dl $ amtr_engine.py --session 3f2c1a9e --report
